+Owner skill: `skill://rust-conventions`. The AI's workspace for one range window started with `--ai` (plan §2 #108–#111, #115): its temporary checkout of the right commit and the agent process running in it; Rust never reads the agent's messages (ACP is the window's). `lib.rs` (the IPC types `AgentRun`, `AgentCommand`, `AgentStartReply`, `CheckoutReply`, `CheckoutLook` — serde tag `kind`, variants as named; `Error`), `workspace.rs` (`Pair` from `yamt-range`'s pair lock; `Workspace`: `prepare` makes or reuses `<pair folder>/checkout`, `start` only after `prepare` with cwd = the checkout and a running agent stopped and reaped first, `send`/`stop` for the current run only, `stop_agent`, `look_job`, `discard` and `end(self)` stop and reap the agent before any removal), `checkout.rs` (made as `checkout.partial` — `clone --shared --no-checkout`, `remote remove origin`, `checkout --detach` the right commit — then renamed to `checkout`, so a `checkout/` is always complete; removed through `checkout.removing`; `remove_when_clean`), `look.rs` (`LookJob::look`: `Missing`, `Clean`, `Changed` = any `git status` entry, ignored files never, or `HEAD` ≠ the right commit; `Unreadable` when git fails or finds another repository than the checkout's own), `process.rs` (the program through `yamt_pipe::find` without project entries — PATH, then the command's home folders — and `Running::start` with `Framing::Lines`), `sweep.rs` (`sweep_leftovers(range_dir, own)`: in every other pair whose lock `PairLock::try_hold` takes, the partial and removing folders and a clean checkout deleted, a changed or unreadable one kept; the right commit read from the folder name `<left>-<right>`; in `own` only the partial and removing folders). `bin/agent-echo.rs`: the tests' line agent (echo, `pwd`, `edit <file>`, `stderr <text>`, `exit <code>`, `huge`, `hold <file>`). Tests in `tests/{checkout,process,sweep}.rs` run real git in temp folders and start the built `agent-echo` where cargo put it. Depends on `yamt-gitio`, `yamt-pipe` and `yamt-range` only among yamt crates; never tauri, never serde_json (arch-check).
